A||||3||Steve Normington||88 Coupes||||1||
Z||000000||Steve Normington||07-31-2001||05:56 PM||||Do the 88 coupes have the same "Lotus" suspension as the Formulas/GTs or did they have the 84-87 suspension?||||reg||1
Z||000001||DRH||07-31-2001||06:03 PM||||Same design as GT and Formula. They are missing the rear swaybar. I saw someone selling a kit to add it somewhere on the internet. <P>I believe they may have had different shocks/struts and spring ratings also. Caster spec is different but I believe all front end parts are the same.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||07-31-2001||08:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Steve Normington:<BR><B>Do the 88 coupes have the same "Lotus" suspension as the Formulas/GTs or did they have the 84-87 suspension?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>All '88 Fieros have the same suspension set-up.  The only difference between the coupe and the GT/Formula suspension is the rear sway bar and front spring rate.  <P>The coupes have softer front springs and no rear sway bar.  Originally they may have had different rated shocks & struts, but all replacements are identical, so that's not a factor.<P>Also,  I know this has been hashed out over and over, but Ltus had nothing to do with the '88 suspension (or any Fiero suspension).<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Steve Normington||08-01-2001||12:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfiero:<BR><B>Also,  I know this has been hashed out over and over, but Ltus had nothing to do with the '88 suspension (or any Fiero suspension).</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hence the bunny ears around Lotus.||||reg||1
